Conforms to named requirment BasicLockable 
https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/named_req/BasicLockable


Consider using a std::unique_lock, std::lock_guard, or std::scoped_lock instead of interacting with the Mutex directly.



std::system_error



Mutex could not be locked within TIMEOUT_MAX milliseconds. see errno for details.



Example //Globalvariablesfortherobot'sodometry,whichtherestoftherobot's
//subsystemswillutilize
doubleodom_x=0.0;
doubleodom_y=0.0;
doubleodom_heading=0.0;

//Thismutexprotectstheodometrydata.Wheneverwereadorwritetothe
//odometrydata,weshouldmakecopiesintothelocalvariables,andread
